 "translation": "Yes, Baba, Sundarlal Babu said, \"There are many things in this world that I don't understand, but I consider that a true Ramrajya where a human being cannot even oppress himself. To be unjust to oneself is as great a sin as being unjust to another. Today too, Lord Ram has expelled Sita from the house just because she had stayed with Ravan. What was Sita's fault in this? Wasn't she also a victim of deceit and fraud, like many of our mothers and sisters? Is this about Sita's truth and untruth, or about the barbarity of the demon Ravan, whose ten heads were human, but one, the biggest head, was that of a donkey?\"",
